WEBVTT

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:04.017
Every species gets a two-part scientific name.

00:00:04.017 --> 00:00:06.745
This is called binomial nomenclature.

00:00:07.458 --> 00:00:15.014
The first word is the genus, and the second is the specific epithet, which identifies the species within that genus.

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:16.903
The house cat is Felis catus.

00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:18.232
The rules:

00:00:18.232 --> 00:00:26.903
the genus is capitalized, the second word is lowercase, and the whole name is written in italics, or underlined when you write it by hand.

00:00:27.603 --> 00:00:28.378
Why bother?

00:00:28.378 --> 00:00:31.194
Common names change from place to place.

00:00:31.194 --> 00:00:37.319
One big cat is called a cougar, a puma, or a mountain lion, depending on where you are.

00:00:37.319 --> 00:00:42.388
Its scientific name, Puma concolor, is the same everywhere in the world.
